  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 132 PM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nThe forecast remains unchanged from the previous package. Warmer \nthan normal temperatures for mid September standards continue \nthrough next week. Sunday through Tuesday, high temperatures are \nforecast to persist in the mid 90s to lower 100s for most spots. \nThis is thanks to upper-level ridging staying over the region. By \nTuesday, the upper-level ridge shifts eastward due to upper-level \ntroughing west and north of the region. As a result, temperatures \nbegin a downward \"cooling\" trend beginning Tuesday lasting through \nthe rest of the week. Highs will cool a few degrees where most \nlocations span in the low to mid 90s. Rain and storm chances (20-\n50%) increase west of the Pecos River and across southeast New \nMexico for much of the work week. Diurnal heating, combined with \nsurface troughing and shortwaves rounding the periphery of the ridge \nwill provide the necessary ascent each afternoon and early evening. \n\nLamberson",
